nNode representing the field "a/b/c" of the schema node (e.g., a text node "value4")', 'description': 'String contains both \'~\' and \'%\'. First the \'~\' replacement yields "a/b%2Fc", then URL decoding yields "a/b/c". This case exercises both special‑character branches sequentially.'}]}, {'group': 'Tilde Present but No Replacement Tokens', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 'no~tilde'}], 'expected': 'JsonNode representing the field "no~tilde" of the schema node (or null if not present)', 'description': 'String contains \'~\' but neither "~1" nor "~0". The replacement code runs but makes no changes, covering the true path of the \'~\' check without altering the key.'}]}, {'group': 'Null Input', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': None}], 'expected': 'NullPointerException', 'description': 'Calling the method with a null argument causes a NPE when `propertyOrIndex.toString()` is invoked. This verifies the method’s behaviour for invalid input.'}]}, {'group': 'Non‑String Object with toString', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 'Boolean.TRUE'}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get("true") – i.e., the child node whose field name is the string representation of the Boolean value', 'description': 'The argument is not a Number, so the method falls back to the else‑branch, calls toString() on the Boolean, and looks up the resulting key "true" in the schema node.'}]}, {'group': 'Double Number Index (truncation)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 2.9}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get(2) – the element at index 2 after the double is truncated to an int', 'description': 'When a Number that is not an integral type is supplied, the method uses intValue(), which truncates the fractional part before indexing the array.'}]}, {'group': 'Negative Number Index', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': -1}], 'expected': 'null (no element at a negative index)', 'description': 'A negative integer is passed; JsonNode.get(-1) returns null, verifying that the method does not perform bounds checking itself.'}]}, {'group': 'Out‑of‑Bounds Index', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 999}], 'expected': 'null (index larger than the array size)', 'description': 'The supplied index exceeds the size of the underlying array node; the method should simply forward the call to node.get(999) which yields null.'}]}, {'group': 'Empty String Property', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': ''}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get("") – typically null unless the schema explicitly contains an empty‑named field', 'description': 'An empty string does not trigger any special‑character handling; it is passed unchanged to node.get("").'}]}, {'group': 'Multiple Tilde Replacements in One String', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 'a~1b~0c'}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get("a/b~c") – after \'~1\' → \'/\' and \'~0\' → \'~\' replacements', 'description': 'The string contains both "~1" and "~0" tokens. The method first replaces "~1" with \'/\', then "~0" with \'~\', yielding the key "a/b~c".'}]}, {'group': 'Percent Decoding Produces Tilde After Decoding (order test)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 'a%7E1b'}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get("a~1b") – percent decoding occurs after the \'~\' check, so no further tilde‑replacement is applied', 'description': 'The original string contains a percent‑encoded \'~\' (%7E). Because the method checks for \'~\' before decoding, the \'~\' token is not replaced; after decoding the string becomes "a~1b" and is used as‑is.'}]}, {'group': 'String with Tilde but No Replacement Tokens and Percent Encoding', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 'no~tilde%20space'}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get("no~tilde space") – \'~\' check runs (no token replacement) then percent decoding turns "%20" into a space', 'description': 'The string contains a \'~\' character that does not form a replacement token, and also contains a percent‑encoded space. The method runs the \'~\' branch (making no changes) and then decodes "%20" to a space.'}]}, {'group': 'Object with Custom toString Returning Escaped Pointer', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'propertyOrIndex', 'value': 'new Object(){ public String toString(){ return "x~1y%2Fz"; } }'}], 'expected': 'JsonNode returned by node.get("x/y/z") – after applying both \'~\' replacement and percent decoding on the custom string', 'description': "An arbitrary object whose toString() yields a JSON‑pointer‑escaped string. The method should treat it like any other non‑Number, performing the '~' and '%' processing steps."}]}]
